-- Forward migration: split full_name into first_name and last_name
BEGIN;

-- Add columns if they don't exist (idempotent)
DO $$
BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.columns 
    WHERE table_name = 'users' AND column_name = 'first_name'
  ) THEN
    ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN first_name VARCHAR(255);
  END IF;

  IF NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.columns 
    WHERE table_name = 'users' AND column_name = 'last_name'
  ) THEN
    ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN last_name VARCHAR(255);
  END IF;
END $$;

-- Backfill: only updates rows where first_name is still NULL (idempotent)
UPDATE users
SET 
  first_name = SPLIT_PART(full_name, ' ', 1),
  last_name = CASE 
    WHEN position(' ' in full_name) > 0 
    THEN SUBSTRING(full_name FROM position(' ' in full_name) + 1)
    ELSE ''
  END
WHERE first_name IS NULL AND full_name IS NOT NULL;

COMMIT;
```

**Idempotency:**
- `IF NOT EXISTS` on column adds → safe to re-run
- `WHERE first_name IS NULL` on backfill → second run touches no rows
- Wrapped in transaction → all-or-nothing

**Re-runnable rollback** (comment out the main migration, run this):
```sql
BEGIN;
DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS first_name;
DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS last_name;
COMMIT;
```

**Integration:** Use with Alembic (`alembic revision --autogenerate`), Flyway (place in `migrations/V1__split_names.sql`), or run directly with `psql -f migration.sql`.

**Edge cases handled:** single-word names → empty last_name; NULL full_name → skipped; re-runs → no duplicate work.
